TheRobotStudio — SO-ARM100 / SO-ARM101
    https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100
    Licensed under Apache-2.0.

    The arm geometry in this repository is derived from the upstream SO-ARM101
    design. Affected files:

        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/base_link.stl
        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/link1_1.stl
        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/link2_1.stl
        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/link3_1.stl
        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/link4_1.stl
        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/visual/link5_1.stl   (partly)
        simulation/so_arm_101_description/meshes/collision/*.stl      (convex
            hulls of the above, generated by scripts/generate_collision_meshes.py)
        community/histology-slide-gripper/mujoco/meshes/arm/*.stl     (byte-identical
            copies of the visual meshes above)

    link5_1.stl fuses the upstream SO-ARM101 wrist with Robonine's
    RB9.01.062.010 Main frame in a single mesh. It is distributed under
    Apache-2.0 in its entirety. See LICENSING.md, section 4.

    The robot description in simulation/so_arm_101_description/urdf/ encodes
    kinematics and inertial parameters for the upstream arm and is likewise
    distributed under Apache-2.0.

    docs/Assembly Guide SO-ARM101.pdf and docs/SO-ARM101 by Robo9.pdf document
    the upstream SO-ARM101 arm rather than the Robonine gripper.


